    "body":  "## Observed drift on main\n\nAudit baseline: `5b666c0ef754ed32fa37c97ce2429f328c70477f`.\n\nThe repository\u0027s current operational docs contradict the implementation and one another:\n\n1. `AGENTS.md` says integrated Compiler v1.0.0 supports only v1alpha4 and v1alpha5 Compiler candidate PR #38 is unmerged.\n2. `README.md` repeats the same obsolete v1alpha4-only Compiler statement and describes the previous Example set (`establish-pdu-session` plus `establish-pdu-session-mas`).\n3. Actual main implementation pins Compiler v2.0.2 and CA-SL v1alpha5:\n   - `experiments/ide-host/vscode/src/compiler-request.mjs`: `COMPILER_VERSION = \"v2.0.2\"`, language target v1alpha5.\n   - `compiler-client.mjs` and `compiler-integration.mjs`: v2.0.2 Worker adapter.\n4. Current sample manifest/tests refer to three Scheme C skills (Create / Modify / Release), while README and large sections of WORK / TRACEABILITY still describe the earlier 2-skill set and earlier compiler release.\n5. `docs/architecture/theia-workbench.md` header correctly labels itself historical and says Classic retired, but its opening paragraph says Classic remains at `/classic/` and later rows describe old CustomEditor / old workspace arrangements. Readers cannot reliably distinguish superseded history from current architecture.\n6. `docs/WORK.md` and `docs/TRACEABILITY.md` contain historical checkpoints that are useful as history, but their current-state summary is not aligned with main and they lack an unambiguous exact-main current snapshot.\n\n## Required change\n\n- Make AGENTS.md and README.md operationally correct for current main, not historical checkpoints.\n- Add one compact current-state section to WORK.md with exact main SHA, deployed SHA, current language target, current Example identities, integrated Compiler version and exact limitations, host support, and current acceptance status.\n- Keep historical records in TRACEABILITY, but label each checkpoint clearly and prevent old entries from being read as current product state.\n- Fix the Theia workbench migration record opening and table labels: historical Classic rows must be explicitly historical; current Theia state must match ADR-0003/0004 and current code.\n- Cross-check all statements against exact owner release refs, current source files and workflow pins. Do not claim Compiler v2.1.0 is integrated until its product chain is merged and verified.\n- Link parent audit #279 and existing Compiler integration Issue #269. Do not create duplicate Compiler implementation work here.\n\n## Acceptance\n- A reviewer can determine current product state from README -\u003e WORK -\u003e TRACEABILITY without encountering contradictory version, Example, host or Classic claims.\n- Every current-state claim links to exact code path, owner contract/release or exact-head workflow evidence.\n- Historical checkpoints remain available but cannot be mistaken for current status.\n- No code behavior is changed by this documentation-only work.\n",
